@@ -5691,3 +5691,9 @@ The critical path for milestone .250:
 - theme: second retro pass for this milestone, triggered by a freshly-raised TIMING INTEGRITY MISMATCH flag; root-caused to the mismatch-detector's own logic rather than to genuinely missed experiment activity
 - key result: honest negative on new experiment commits (still 0), but the "mismatch" itself is very likely a false positive -- `scripts/research_conductor.py`'s check builds `milestone_marker = f"milestone {current}"` yet tests bare `current in changelog_text`, so it fires on the prior retro pass's own auto-appended changelog line (confirmed via grep: exactly one hit, that entry) rather than on genuine untracked experiment evidence; every retro pass is required to append a changelog line naming the milestone, so any milestone with 2+ retro passes will always trip this flag regardless of real activity. Supplementary `ops/conductor-log.md` read confirms no PHASE task attempts between the 10:35 UTC success and 11:43 UTC, only a failed 1201s Codex CLI "Plan next milestone" idle-timeout (the fourth such stall logged today)
 - acceptance: 0/0 criteria met -- no experiment criteria were present in the supplied timing data this pass; the detector root-cause is a supplementary operational diagnosis, not a milestone research deliverable
+
+### Milestone 2026.07.475 (third same-day pass -- live .476 activation-refusal loop identified as the real bottleneck)
+- exp_range: no data available this milestone per the supplied TIMING DATA block (unchanged zero; not derivable from the timing block itself)
+- theme: third retro-generation pass for this milestone number; re-confirms the second pass's self-referential timing-mismatch diagnosis with fresh evidence, then locates the actual live operational blocker via a supplementary conductor-log read
+- key result: honest negative on the locked fields (still 0 experiments, 0 wall-time minutes, 0 compute-bound tasks), and the timing_integrity_mismatch self-referential-detector diagnosis from the prior pass is unchanged (`scripts/research_conductor.py:2907-2908` still compares bare `current` instead of `milestone_marker`) -- but this pass's supplementary `ops/conductor-log.md` read (outside the TIMING DATA block) found the conductor has been stuck since at least 12:52 UTC in a tight activation-refusal loop for the *next* milestone, 2026.07.476: 65 consecutive `Activation REFUSED ... WRONG_MECHANISM_PRECONDITION` entries through 15:12 UTC, still recurring, roughly one failed attempt every 2 minutes with zero forward progress, and `research-roadmap.yaml` still pinned at `milestone: 2026.07.475`. This fully explains why three consecutive .475 retro passes all show zero new experiments -- the conductor isn't idle, it is looping on a malformed .476 draft against a HARD, no-override exclusion-manifest check (KV260 `/dev/mmcblk` retired-precondition guard) that cannot self-resolve without a planner- or lint-level fix
+- acceptance: 0/0 criteria met -- no experiment criteria were present in the supplied timing data; the live activation-loop finding is supplementary operational diagnosis (this retro task's scope forbids editing scripts/research_conductor.py or research-roadmap.yaml), escalation to ops/known-issues.md is recommended as the next step
